<blockquote class="uncited"><div>what I've understand for that thread is that he first flashed the radio with the proper donor firmware file and with the normal opengd77 for uv380 but after that the screen was completely black, so he decided to restored flash and thinking to go back to the original firmware, but instead of that he flashed again opengd77 but this time the Japanese version for uv380 and the same donor file, and that fixed the screen.</div></blockquote>The only difference with the Japanese version is that the font bitmap contains Japanese characters.<br><br>So probably he just did things correctly the last time he flashed the radio, but he also happened to use the Japanese version when he did things correctly.<br><br>The CPS won't flash the official firmware correctly, even for the donor firmware, onto the MD9600, because the official firmware file is encrypted but the OpenGD77 firmware isn't.<br><br>Possibly we should change the CPS to prevent it allowing people to flash the official donor firmware, by checking that the firmware they select contains the string text OpenGD77.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Jan 31, 2025 6:05 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
