<blockquote class="uncited"><div>the fact one firmware turn the screen white, and another turn the screen all black makes me think it's not a ribbon cable connection problem which I'm aware of.<br><br>  I still think it's newer hardware ver....</div></blockquote>Please can you explain the problem again.<br><br>IIRC you are sawing that the screen is either "black" or "white" depending on which firmware target you install,  but you sy the screen is not "valid"<br><br>What does "valid" mean in this context?<br><br><br>Also I presume when you say back or white, you are referring to whether the backlight is illuminated or not.<br>I.e the difference with the 10w radios is that the manufacturer changed the hardware design and swapped the PA enable and backlight signals from the MCU ( CPU )<br><br>If you are sawing that on firmware e,g. The 10W illuminates the backlight, but the screen is blank, then it's still possible that you have a connection problem, i.e with the pixel data connections<br><br>If you can't find an official firmware version that works, it points to the same conclusion <br><br>Often the ribbon cable to the screen gets disturbed when people plug in the USB cable to update the firmware... This has happened to multiple people fairly recently<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Jan 30, 2025 7:40 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
